    "body": "You begin with a liquid, Mass \\textbf{M = 2.5 kg} at room temperature in a not very well insulated container. You stir the liquid until a thermometer shows that its temperature increased by $\\triangle T$ = \\textbf{0.4 K}. In the process you did work \\textbf{W = 5300 J} on the liquid by stirring it. The specific heat capacity of the liquid is \\textbf{C = 3800 J/Kg/K.}\n\nWhat is the \\textbf{magnitude of the heat transfer} $\\mid Q \\mid$, from the liquid to its surroundings due to a temperature difference that occured while you stirred? \\textbf{Select the closest answer.}",
